    "created_at": "2020-03-04T17:57:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-03-04T17:57:56Z",
    "body": "<del>@tkent-google, what was the intent here?</del> <ins>Sorry @tkent-google, I misremembered. You generalized the autofocus attribute, not the inputmode attribute. Still, your perspective would be appreciated :).</ins>\r\n\r\nI think the text as-written makes _sense_; you could vary the inputmode depending on what part of the editing host is being edited. For example\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<div contenteditable>\r\n  <div inputmode=numeric>12345</div>\r\n  <div inputmode=url>https://example.com/</div>\r\n</div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut I can understand if this is not something browsers want to implement.\r\n\r\nAnd, it seems like it should at the very least also be supported _on_ the editing host, not just elements inside of it.\r\n\r\nOther note: Any changes here should apply to enterkeyhint as well, which seems to use the same model. Those two seem to use a different model from autocapitalize, which does not work on contenteditable per spec today... I wonder if we should try to unify all three.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
