    "created_at": "2020-03-04T20:03:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-03-04T20:03:26Z",
    "body": "> I think the text as-written makes sense; you could vary the inputmode depending on what part of the editing host is being edited. For example\r\n> ```\r\n> <div contenteditable>\r\n>  <div inputmode=numeric>12345</div>\r\n>  <div inputmode=url>https://example.com/</div>\r\n> </div>\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nExcept selection run across those two elements then what? Also, it’s not a thing that browser can preserve those div’s in any consistent manner e.g. when the user deletes the new line between the numbers & URL.\r\n\r\nAs the current spec test reads, it’s at best so under-specified that it’s not implementable. As I read it, it just doesn’t make any sense.",
